{{also|đách}}
==German==

===Etymology===
Old High German ''[[dach]]'', originally *''dak'', compare Dutch ''[[dak]]''. Cognate with Danish {{term|tag||roof|lang=da}}, English {{term|thack|lang=en}}, Old Norse {{term|þak||thatch, roof|lang=non}}. Akin to Latin {{term|toga||garment}} and Ancient Greek {{term|στέγος|tr=stegos||roof|lang=grc}}.

